WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:14.670 --> 00:00:19.610
Gianni Versace was a brilliant businessman
who took his humble beginnings and built a

00:00:19.610 --> 00:00:21.880
multi-billion dollar fashion empire.

00:00:21.880 --> 00:00:27.360
He became a celebrity designer, and his company’s
famous Medusa logo is recognized around the

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:28.360
world.

00:00:28.360 --> 00:00:33.940
But in 1997, his life was cut short when he
became the victim of a serial killer.

00:00:33.940 --> 00:00:38.980
On today’s Biographics, we will tell the
inspiring story of Gianni Versace’s rags-to-riches

00:00:38.980 --> 00:00:43.011
success story, as well as the shocking twist
that ended his life.

00:00:43.011 --> 00:00:52.500
Life in Italy
Gianni Versace was born on December 2nd, 1946

00:00:52.500 --> 00:01:00.710
in Reggio Calabria, Italy.

00:01:00.710 --> 00:01:05.350
He had two older siblings; a brother named
Santo, and a sister named Francesca.

00:01:05.350 --> 00:01:07.710
His parents ran a dressmaking business.

00:01:07.710 --> 00:01:12.950
His father handled the sales, while his mother
managed their staff with sewing and assembly.

00:01:12.950 --> 00:01:17.920
Tragically, his older sister Francesca died
at 12 years old from a tetanus infection that

00:01:17.920 --> 00:01:18.920
had gone untreated.

00:01:18.920 --> 00:01:23.380
When he was 10, his parents decided to have
another child, and his younger sister Donatella

00:01:23.380 --> 00:01:24.380
was born.

00:01:24.380 --> 00:01:28.619
Gianni treasured baby Donatella, and they
would grow up to become best friends.

00:01:28.619 --> 00:01:33.079
All his life, Gianni Versace loved classical
music and opera, and he had a dream of becoming

00:01:33.079 --> 00:01:34.390
a professional composer.

00:01:34.390 --> 00:01:38.719
However, his parents needed help around the
dress shop, and he was forced to give up his

00:01:38.719 --> 00:01:41.620
dream in order to enter the family business.

00:01:41.620 --> 00:01:48.260
He learned how to select fabrics, sew, sketch,
and create dress patterns for new designs.

00:01:48.260 --> 00:01:51.869
During his apprenticeship, Gianni paid close
attention to his parents.

00:01:51.869 --> 00:01:55.710
They knew how to make their clients feel comfortable,
and when these women looked in the mirror

00:01:55.710 --> 00:02:00.729
with their new dresses, his mother made sure
they felt like they were the most important

00:02:00.729 --> 00:02:02.310
person in the room.

00:02:02.310 --> 00:02:06.069
Since his parents were both so busy running
the family business, he spent a lot of time

00:02:06.069 --> 00:02:07.630
babysitting little Donatella.

00:02:07.630 --> 00:02:10.990
One day, Gianni took his sister to visit the
Roman Colosseum.

00:02:10.990 --> 00:02:15.140
This is when he came face-to-face with the
statue of Medusa.

00:02:15.140 --> 00:02:19.310
He was so entranced by this terrifying woman
with hair made of snakes.

00:02:19.310 --> 00:02:23.560
In school, Versace was studying Greek and
Latin, and he began to learn more about the

00:02:23.560 --> 00:02:25.220
original mythology of Medusa.

00:02:25.220 --> 00:02:31.150
He didn’t know it at the time, but this
legend would eventually make a huge impact

00:02:31.150 --> 00:02:32.670
on his future company.

00:02:32.670 --> 00:02:37.540
Most people know the legend of the monster
whose eyes could turn men to stone.

00:02:37.540 --> 00:02:42.930
Maybe you already know the story of Perseus,
who chopped off her head and used it as his

00:02:42.930 --> 00:02:43.930
own personal shield.

00:02:43.930 --> 00:02:48.189
But Medusa’s backstory is actually far more
complex.

00:02:48.189 --> 00:02:51.370
Medusa was born a mortal woman, and she worked
in the temple of Athena.

00:02:51.370 --> 00:02:55.850
These priestesses swore a vow of chastity,
and covered up in modest attire.

00:02:55.850 --> 00:03:01.670
Even so, Medusa was so beautiful, that news
spread about her, and Athena became jealous

00:03:01.670 --> 00:03:02.670
and resentful.

00:03:02.670 --> 00:03:04.630
The god of the sea, Poseidon, lusted after
Medusa.

00:03:04.630 --> 00:03:10.310
One day, she was walking along the shore,
and Poseidon emerged from the sea to kidnap

00:03:10.310 --> 00:03:12.370
and forced himself upon her.

00:03:12.370 --> 00:03:17.050
Instead of acknowledging that she was a victim,
Athena claimed that Medusa was asking for

00:03:17.050 --> 00:03:19.800
it, and violated her oath of purity.

00:03:19.800 --> 00:03:22.790
Athena transformed her into a monster with
snakes for hair.

00:03:22.790 --> 00:03:28.510
Now, every time she looked at a man, he would
turn to stone, which guaranteed that she would

00:03:28.510 --> 00:03:30.010
be alone forever.

00:03:30.010 --> 00:03:34.950
The true moral of the story was that even
the gods were not above petty jealousy.

00:03:34.950 --> 00:03:38.390
Gianni Versace was completely inspired by
the story of Medusa.

00:03:38.390 --> 00:03:42.890
In most artistic renderings, she is always
either naked or just-barely clothed.

00:03:42.890 --> 00:03:47.760
With her curse came great power, because there
was no way she would ever be attacked by a

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:48.760
man again.

00:03:48.760 --> 00:03:51.280
For Medusa, there was no need to dress modestly.

00:03:51.280 --> 00:03:56.120
Versace would sketch pictures of the kinds
of dresses he imagined Medusa would wear.

00:03:56.120 --> 00:03:59.600
These clothes had bright colors, and showed
off a woman’s curves.

00:03:59.600 --> 00:04:02.349
He carried on this style for the rest of his
career.

00:04:02.349 --> 00:04:07.310
Years later, the face of Medusa became the
logo of the Versace brand.

00:04:07.310 --> 00:04:14.329
Growing the Versace Brand
At age 26, Gianni Versace decided that he

00:04:14.329 --> 00:04:18.510
wanted to take his skills to the next level
by moving to Milan and immersing himself in

00:04:18.510 --> 00:04:20.320
the world of luxury fashion.

00:04:20.320 --> 00:04:23.710
He got a job for a clothing manufacturer named
Genny’s.

00:04:23.710 --> 00:04:29.140
While he was under their employment, he was
able to design two of his own lines of ready-to-wear

00:04:29.140 --> 00:04:30.140
clothing.

00:04:30.140 --> 00:04:34.000
After building this portfolio, he began working
for other well-established Italian fashion

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:35.060
houses.

00:04:35.060 --> 00:04:40.500
Versace spent 6 years living and working in
Milan gaining valuable experience and networking

00:04:40.500 --> 00:04:42.560
with people in the fashion industry.

00:04:42.560 --> 00:04:47.410
He eventually made a collection of his original
pieces, and they were on display at the Palazzo

00:04:47.410 --> 00:04:49.900
della Permanente Art Museum.

00:04:49.900 --> 00:04:55.040
This exhibit was a smashing success, and it
got him enough inquiries from new clients

00:04:55.040 --> 00:04:58.500
to where he could start selling pieces direct
to customers.

00:04:58.500 --> 00:05:02.650
In 1978, when Gianni Versace was 32 years
old, he was finally ready to open his first

00:05:02.650 --> 00:05:06.050
boutique in Milan’s famous Via della Spiga
shopping district.

00:05:06.050 --> 00:05:11.940
At first, his clothing store was just a single
rack of dresses, and yet his talent was still

00:05:11.940 --> 00:05:14.920
enough to have women coming in to see his
creations.

00:05:14.920 --> 00:05:22.450
Milan is one of the fashion capitals of the
world, so the competition is fierce.

00:05:22.450 --> 00:05:28.010
Designers open boutiques all the time, only
for them to not turn a profit, and yet Versace

00:05:28.010 --> 00:05:29.670
had the skills to push through.

00:05:29.670 --> 00:05:33.980
In order to be successful in any business-
not just fashion- you have to understand your

00:05:33.980 --> 00:05:34.980
customer.

00:05:34.980 --> 00:05:35.980
Who are they?

00:05:35.980 --> 00:05:36.980
And what do they need to make their life better?

00:05:36.980 --> 00:05:41.400
For Gianni Versace, he wanted to design clothes
for men and women who were sexy, confident,

00:05:41.400 --> 00:05:42.400
and powerful.

00:05:42.400 --> 00:05:46.730
And to him, the one person who exemplified
all of the qualities was his younger sister

00:05:46.730 --> 00:05:47.730
Donatella.

00:05:47.730 --> 00:05:51.830
She has a keen eye for style, and she was
not afraid to share her criticism of her older

00:05:51.830 --> 00:05:52.990
brother’s work.

00:05:52.990 --> 00:05:57.630
When Gianni designed something that was ugly,
Donatella would tell him immediately.

00:05:57.630 --> 00:06:02.790
Eventually, Gianni learned Donatella’s taste
in clothing, and she became his muse.

00:06:02.790 --> 00:06:07.450
During several interviews, Gianni shared how
much Donatella inspired him, saying, “She

00:06:07.450 --> 00:06:08.930
is my first customer.”

00:06:08.930 --> 00:06:12.330
But Donatella wasn’t just the artistic inspiration.

00:06:12.330 --> 00:06:16.440
Gianni made her the vice-president of the
corporation when she was still in her early

00:06:16.440 --> 00:06:18.970
20’s, and his older brother Santo was the
president.

00:06:18.970 --> 00:06:22.970
Even though she was technically vice-president,
Donatella was still very young, and she was

00:06:22.970 --> 00:06:25.970
figuring out what she wanted to do with her
life.

00:06:25.970 --> 00:06:29.280
Ultimately, she decided that she wanted to
be a fashion designer, as well.

00:06:29.280 --> 00:06:35.190
So Gianni started a second brand called Versus,
which existed as a subsidiary of the larger

00:06:35.190 --> 00:06:36.520
Versace corporation.

00:06:36.520 --> 00:06:40.861
Donatella did all of the designs, and she
began to learn all of the ins an outs of the

00:06:40.861 --> 00:06:45.450
fashion business, just like Gianni had when
working in Milan.

00:06:45.450 --> 00:06:50.310
To an untrained eye, someone might look at
the Versace family’s designs and assume

00:06:50.310 --> 00:06:53.380
that not much thought went into it at all.

00:06:53.380 --> 00:06:57.621
Many people have even gone as far as to say
that they are overly sexualized, and the whole

00:06:57.621 --> 00:07:00.590
point of the fashion line was to exploit women’s
bodies.

00:07:00.590 --> 00:07:02.330
He got a lot of push-back.

00:07:02.330 --> 00:07:05.450
Many people said that his dresses were too
vulgar.

00:07:05.450 --> 00:07:11.610
A phrase that became famous was: "Armani dresses
the wife, Versace dresses the mistress."

00:07:11.610 --> 00:07:15.770
During an interview with Charlie Rose, Versace
responded to these criticisms with a quote

00:07:15.770 --> 00:07:20.890
from Friedrich Nietzsche, “Those who know
that they are profound strive for clarity.”

00:07:20.890 --> 00:07:25.250
As in- He has the ability to design anything
he wants, and he could do it well.

00:07:25.250 --> 00:07:29.120
But he was choosing to design this way for
a very good reason.

00:07:29.120 --> 00:07:33.510
Versace hated the fact that somewhere along
the course of human history, it was decided

00:07:33.510 --> 00:07:40.040
that men were expected to wear a suit and
tie, and anything else was deemed to be unprofessional.

00:07:40.040 --> 00:07:44.000
And for women with beautiful bodies, they
had to hide them away in order to be taken

00:07:44.000 --> 00:07:45.000
seriously.

00:07:45.000 --> 00:07:48.580
He knew that so many people out there wanted
to express themselves through fashion, and

00:07:48.580 --> 00:07:53.200
they were holding back from going outside
of the box out of fear of being judged.

00:07:53.200 --> 00:07:55.890
He said, “Don't be into trends.

00:07:55.890 --> 00:07:57.760
Don't make fashion own you.

00:07:57.760 --> 00:08:03.790
But you decide what you are, what you want
to express by the way you dress, and the way

00:08:03.790 --> 00:08:05.690
to live.”

00:08:05.690 --> 00:08:12.790
Fame and Fortune
Combined with his visionary fashion sense,

00:08:12.790 --> 00:08:14.560
Versace was also a brilliant businessman.

00:08:14.560 --> 00:08:18.330
At the time, other major fashion brands weren’t
bothering to head to eastern countries.

00:08:18.330 --> 00:08:22.020
They were trying to focus on the west, where
they believed most of the money was.

00:08:22.020 --> 00:08:25.410
Versace opened up his first shop in China
in 1979.

00:08:25.410 --> 00:08:29.990
Hindsight is always 20/20, of course, but
we know today that establishing himself in

00:08:29.990 --> 00:08:32.630
China was an incredibly smart move.

00:08:32.630 --> 00:08:35.320
He was always ten steps ahead of the competition.

00:08:35.320 --> 00:08:40.390
In the 1980’s and early 90’s, Gianni Versace
continued to open more of his shops all over

00:08:40.390 --> 00:08:42.830
the world, and his designs became famous.

00:08:42.830 --> 00:08:48.149
He began to dress some of the biggest celebrities
in the world at the time, like Elton John,

00:08:48.149 --> 00:08:49.990
Princess Diana, Cher, and Madonna.

00:08:49.990 --> 00:08:56.450
Honestly, there were so many celebrity clients
that Versace worked with, we cannot possibly

00:08:56.450 --> 00:08:57.670
mention them all in this video.

00:08:57.670 --> 00:09:00.209
He also designed costumes for the opera called
Capriccio.

00:09:00.209 --> 00:09:04.160
So, even if he could not be a composer, he
was still able to keep his love of music in

00:09:04.160 --> 00:09:08.300
his life by dressing both classical singers
and rock stars alike.

00:09:08.300 --> 00:09:11.731
Getting celebrity endorsements are critical
for the success of a business, but it can

00:09:11.731 --> 00:09:17.660
sometimes just be a flash in the pan, especially
in the world of fashion.

00:09:17.660 --> 00:09:22.290
Versace was smart enough to know that in order
for his company to last for future generations,

00:09:22.290 --> 00:09:23.290
it needed longevity.

00:09:23.290 --> 00:09:27.519
We aren’t going to name names, here, but
there are some luxury fashion companies out

00:09:27.519 --> 00:09:31.920
there that have a very snobbish attitude about
who they want their ideal customer to be.

00:09:31.920 --> 00:09:36.040
They refuse to make products that are affordable
to the middle-class, because they only want

00:09:36.040 --> 00:09:38.290
the richest people to represent them.

00:09:38.290 --> 00:09:42.699
Some luxury brands actually burn their products,
because they would rather destroy those pieces

00:09:42.699 --> 00:09:47.610
than ever put them on clearance, which would
allow mear peasants to be able to afford to

00:09:47.610 --> 00:09:49.600
wear their brand.

00:09:49.600 --> 00:09:52.960
For Versace, though, he felt the exact opposite.

00:09:52.960 --> 00:09:55.940
He wanted to make his brand more accessible
to a wider audience.

00:09:55.940 --> 00:10:00.889
And he knew that by opening it up to anyone,
it would ultimately make the company more

00:10:00.889 --> 00:10:01.889
successful.

00:10:01.889 --> 00:10:06.980
He began to sell smaller luxury accessories
like jewelry, wallets, perfume, and home decor

00:10:06.980 --> 00:10:07.980
items.

00:10:07.980 --> 00:10:11.810
While some luxury brands cost thousands of
dollars for a purse or dress, someone can

00:10:11.810 --> 00:10:14.660
buy a Versace piece for just a few hundred
dollars.

00:10:14.660 --> 00:10:18.230
In turn, his brand’s Medusa logo was seen
by more people.

00:10:18.230 --> 00:10:21.360
It’s almost needless to say that at this
point in his life, Gianni Versace had become

00:10:21.360 --> 00:10:22.360
a multi-millionaire.

00:10:22.360 --> 00:10:23.790
Personal Life
In 1982, Versace’s fashion business was

00:10:23.790 --> 00:10:24.790
in full swing.

00:10:24.790 --> 00:10:26.459
He fell in love with a fashion model named
Antonio D'Amico.

00:10:26.459 --> 00:10:29.899
Gay marriage was not legal at the time, but
they were life partners for 15 years.

00:10:29.899 --> 00:10:59.490
D’Amico and Versace would spend time in
Milan, and travel around the world together.

00:10:59.490 --> 00:13:15.259
In 1992, they were on a flight to Cuba, and
had a layover in Miami.

00:13:15.259 --> 00:13:19.589
Gianni asked their driver to bring him and
Antonio around, just to see what Miami was

00:13:19.589 --> 00:13:20.589
like.

00:13:20.589 --> 00:13:24.059
Once he saw it, he was shocked at how beautiful
it was, and he knew that he had accidentally

00:13:24.059 --> 00:13:26.649
found the location of his new home.

00:13:26.649 --> 00:13:30.740
After visiting an area of the city called
South Beach, he saw that there was a community

00:13:30.740 --> 00:13:34.329
of young gay men who were not afraid to show
who they truly were.

00:13:34.329 --> 00:13:38.160
Growing up in Europe, this level of honesty
and freedom to live out of the closet was

00:13:38.160 --> 00:13:42.720
refreshing to Versace, and he was convinced
that this truly was the perfect place for

00:13:42.720 --> 00:13:44.069
him and D’Amico to live.

00:13:44.069 --> 00:13:48.069
As he was walking along the beach, Versace
spotted a large Mediterranean Revival style

00:13:48.069 --> 00:13:53.080
mansion with a statue of the goddess of love-
Aphrodite- sitting in the front courtyard.

00:13:53.080 --> 00:13:56.149
He was still a die-hard mythology nerd deep
down, of course.

00:13:56.149 --> 00:13:59.610
So once he saw one of this favorite characters,
he took this as a sign that this was going

00:13:59.610 --> 00:14:01.790
to be his future home with D’Amico.

00:14:01.790 --> 00:14:05.560
He bought this property, and called it La
Casa Casuarina.

00:14:05.560 --> 00:14:10.180
The home is truly a slice of Italy sitting
in the middle of Miami.

00:14:10.180 --> 00:14:13.769
Even though he was now in his late 40’s
and settled into his forever-home, Gianni

00:14:13.769 --> 00:14:15.600
Versace was far from retirement.

00:14:15.600 --> 00:14:19.459
He still loved running his business, and he
was eager to continuing improving his designs.

00:14:19.459 --> 00:14:23.610
During an interview, he once said, “It’s
like oxygen for me.

00:14:23.610 --> 00:14:24.970
I love doing fashion.”

00:14:24.970 --> 00:14:29.249
He understood that what is popular in fashion
today might change by tomorrow.

00:14:29.249 --> 00:14:31.589
So he would frequent Miami nightclubs.

00:14:31.589 --> 00:14:34.640
Instead of dancing in the crowd, he often
sat on the sidelines so that he could pay

00:14:34.640 --> 00:14:37.399
attention and study these young, beautiful
people.

00:14:37.399 --> 00:14:41.529
According to D’Amico, Versace never drank
alcohol, even in this social setting, because

00:14:41.529 --> 00:14:44.889
he wanted to stay sober in order to truly
be present in the moment.

00:14:44.889 --> 00:14:47.889
Everyone in the community began to recognize
and respect him.

00:14:47.889 --> 00:14:51.690
Some say that he was the “unofficial mayor
of South Beach”

00:14:51.690 --> 00:14:55.910
Even though everyone in his personal life
knew about his sexual orientation, Versace

00:14:55.910 --> 00:14:57.029
still kept it a secret.

00:14:57.029 --> 00:15:01.089
He and Donatella had been considering taking
the company public on the stock market, and

00:15:01.089 --> 00:15:05.019
they were afraid that shareholders would not
want to invest if they knew that he was gay.

00:15:05.019 --> 00:15:09.040
But in 1995, Gianni Versace made the decision
to finally came out of the closet.

00:15:09.040 --> 00:15:13.040
He publicly announced that he was gay, and
had been in a long-term relationship with

00:15:13.040 --> 00:15:14.529
Antonio D’Amico.

00:15:14.529 --> 00:15:18.610
Gianni Versace was truly modest, and he never
acted as if he was better than anyone else

00:15:18.610 --> 00:15:22.499
living in Miami, and even after he had reached
a level of celebrity.

00:15:22.499 --> 00:15:25.950
He continued spending time out in the world
among normal people.

00:15:25.950 --> 00:15:30.690
While his mindset was admirable, this would
turn out to be a tragic mistake.

00:15:30.690 --> 00:15:33.860
The Assassination
In July of 1997, Versace was now 50 years

00:15:33.860 --> 00:15:34.860
old.

00:15:34.860 --> 00:15:39.130
His designs were on the covers of magazines,
he had been on TV on multiple occasions.

00:15:39.130 --> 00:15:42.370
Everyone knew that he was a multi-millionaire,
but he still ran his own errands around town,

00:15:42.370 --> 00:15:43.540
just like anyone else.

00:15:43.540 --> 00:15:47.600
Versace was well-loved in Miami, always saying
“hello” and being friendly towards the

00:15:47.600 --> 00:15:48.600
locals.

00:15:48.600 --> 00:15:52.189
According to Antonio D’Amico, Versace was
always willing to help other people, and described

00:15:52.189 --> 00:15:54.860
him as being one of the sweetest men who ever
lived.

00:15:54.860 --> 00:15:58.120
So he did not make any enemies, and therefore
truly felt safe.

00:15:58.120 --> 00:16:02.369
Ironically, Versace often told his friends
that he believed that America was a lot safer

00:16:02.369 --> 00:16:06.069
than Italy- mainly because the mafia reigned
in his hometown of Calabria.

00:16:06.069 --> 00:16:10.940
On the morning of July 15, 1997, Gianni Versace
left his home to get a cup of coffee and the

00:16:10.940 --> 00:16:13.940
newest issues of The New Yorker and Vogue
magazine.

00:16:13.940 --> 00:16:17.980
Versace would never expect that he had a stalker
who had been studying his every move.

00:16:17.980 --> 00:16:21.600
He was unlocking his front gate, with his
back turned to the street, when a serial killer

00:16:21.600 --> 00:16:25.429
named Andrew Cunanan shot him twice in the
back of the head.

00:16:25.429 --> 00:16:29.720
With a strange twist of fate, the bullet went
through Versace’s body and hit a nearby

00:16:29.720 --> 00:16:32.779
dove, which fell to the ground next to Versace’s
body.

00:16:32.779 --> 00:16:36.759
Antonio D’Amico was home, waiting for his
partner to return with his coffee and magazines.

00:16:36.759 --> 00:16:38.999
He said, “I heard the shot.

00:16:38.999 --> 00:16:39.999
My heart just stopped.

00:16:39.999 --> 00:16:47.519
So I ran out, and I saw Gianni lying on the
stairs in blood.”

00:16:47.519 --> 00:16:51.110
When the police arrived, they saw the dead
bird lying on the ground next to Versace.

00:16:51.110 --> 00:16:54.389
They assumed the dove may be a symbol that
this was a hit by the Italian mob.

00:16:54.389 --> 00:16:59.019
But they eventually figured out that the culprit
was Andrew Cunanan, who had already appeared

00:16:59.019 --> 00:17:01.990
on America’s Most Wanted for killing four
other men.

00:17:01.990 --> 00:17:05.580
During the press conference, it was announced
to the press that Gianni Versace had no connection

00:17:05.580 --> 00:17:07.730
to Andrew Cunanan whatsoever.

00:17:07.730 --> 00:17:10.959
The FBI had to investigate the connection
between the two.

00:17:10.959 --> 00:17:14.500
Eight days later, they finally caught up with
Andrew Cunanan, and he was surrounded by the

00:17:14.500 --> 00:17:15.500
police.

00:17:15.500 --> 00:17:18.120
He shot himself in the head before the FBI
had a chance to question him.

00:17:18.120 --> 00:17:22.730
So no one knows his true motivation behind
killing a famous fashion designer.

00:17:22.730 --> 00:17:26.890
Before assassinating Gianni Versace, Andrew
Cunanan was an escort who catered to older,

00:17:26.890 --> 00:17:27.890
wealthy men.

00:17:27.890 --> 00:17:31.010
Cunanan had a genius IQ, and he had a photographic
memory.

00:17:31.010 --> 00:17:34.970
His parents spoiled him rotten, and gave him
absolutely anything he could ever ask for.

00:17:34.970 --> 00:17:38.080
Andrew was made to believe that he was better
than everyone else.

00:17:38.080 --> 00:17:42.030
Surprise, surprise- he became a narcissist
and a sociopath.

00:17:42.030 --> 00:17:45.140
Andrew Cunanan was the polar opposite of Gianni
Versace.

00:17:45.140 --> 00:17:49.450
He truly did feel that he was entitled to
have the finest things in life handed to him

00:17:49.450 --> 00:17:50.700
without working for it.

00:17:50.700 --> 00:17:55.920
Cunanan was incapable of empathy for other
people, and he also became a compulsive liar-

00:17:55.920 --> 00:18:00.730
telling everyone he met a different story
about his name, career, parents, and so much

00:18:00.730 --> 00:18:01.730
more.

00:18:01.730 --> 00:18:06.030
Some speculate that after learning that Gianni
Versace was gay, Andrew Cunanan began stalking

00:18:06.030 --> 00:18:10.610
Versace, and that he may have approached him
with the intention of becoming his escort.

00:18:10.610 --> 00:18:14.530
In 2018, TV series “American Crime Story:
The Assassination of Gianni Versace” does

00:18:14.530 --> 00:18:18.840
a lot of speculating into the possibility
that they may have met before the assassination.

00:18:18.840 --> 00:18:21.540
But if you watch it, do so with a grain of
salt.

00:18:21.540 --> 00:18:26.610
According to an interview with Antonio D’Amico,
he was insulted by much of what the show claimed,

00:18:26.610 --> 00:18:29.980
and he believes that Versace never met Cunanan
before.

00:18:29.980 --> 00:18:33.320
After this autopsy, it was revealed that Gianni
Versace had HIV.

00:18:33.320 --> 00:18:36.820
Because of this, many speculate that D’Amico
must have been unfaithful, or that they had

00:18:36.820 --> 00:18:38.070
an open relationship.

00:18:38.070 --> 00:18:43.360
But what we do know for certain is that Donatella
Versace did not like Antonio D’Amico at

00:18:43.360 --> 00:18:44.360
all.

00:18:44.360 --> 00:18:48.290
In his will, Gianni Versace left D’Amico
an allowance of $57,000 a month, and that

00:18:48.290 --> 00:18:51.290
he had the right to live any of the Versace
family mansions around the world.

00:18:51.290 --> 00:18:55.490
But Donatella was in charge of the estate,
and she did not want D’Amico to have so

00:18:55.490 --> 00:18:57.570
much of her brother’s money and properties.

00:18:57.570 --> 00:18:59.110
So they had to go to court.

00:18:59.110 --> 00:19:03.280
D’Amico left with a lump sum for his inheritance,
and decided not to fight over living in the

00:19:03.280 --> 00:19:04.280
mansion.

00:19:04.280 --> 00:19:07.740
After all, it was the place where he witnesses
the love of his life shot and killed.

00:19:07.740 --> 00:19:15.190
It was the last place he wanted to live.

00:19:15.190 --> 00:19:18.910
Legacy
Donatella Versace took over creative control

00:19:18.910 --> 00:19:20.480
of the company after Gianni was killed.

00:19:20.480 --> 00:19:25.260
She and her older brother Santo agreed that
they would keep the company private and family-owned.

00:19:25.260 --> 00:19:28.420
Without her brother there, she was now the
one and only designer who had to carry on

00:19:28.420 --> 00:19:29.420
the Versace legacy.

00:19:29.420 --> 00:19:32.890
Years later, she spoke at Oxford University
about how she managed to continue to grow

00:19:32.890 --> 00:19:35.610
the brand, even after her brother’s death.

00:19:35.610 --> 00:19:39.740
She said, “Fashion is a weapon that you
can use when you need it...My own look makes

00:19:39.740 --> 00:19:41.210
people think I'm tough.

00:19:41.210 --> 00:19:44.710
It's like armour that was useful to me in
the first years after Gianni's death.

00:19:44.710 --> 00:19:48.850
It was difficult to live that pain in public
- and to be compared to him when he was the

00:19:48.850 --> 00:19:51.930
genius and I was only ever the accessory.

00:19:51.930 --> 00:19:55.250
It was hard to hear people constantly say
'will she make it?'”.

00:19:55.250 --> 00:19:56.330
But she did.

00:19:56.330 --> 00:19:59.920
Sources vary as to how much the Versace brand
was worth at the time of his death, because

00:19:59.920 --> 00:20:02.850
the sales of his clothing truly go down after
he came out of the closet.

00:20:02.850 --> 00:20:05.730
Reports of its value vary between $400 and
$700 million.

00:20:05.730 --> 00:20:10.770
For the next 11 years, Donatella continued
to grow the company, and in 2018, the Versace

00:20:10.770 --> 00:20:15.100
brand was purchased by Michael Kors for $2.1
Billion.

00:20:15.100 --> 00:20:19.420
The La Casa Casuarina mansion has been turned
into a hotel and event venue simply called

00:20:19.420 --> 00:20:23.750
“The Villa”, and it continues to be a
popular Miami tourist attraction to this day.

00:20:23.750 --> 00:20:27.430
Even years after his death, the Versace brand
is still going strong to this very day, and

00:20:27.430 --> 00:20:46.100
it will most likely be around for 
a long time.

